      "content": "The International Monetary Fund's (IMF) 2010 bailout of Greece is a prime example of a global organization's policies threatening a country's domestic control. The IMF's strict austerity measures, imposed under the guise of economic stability, led to widespread social unrest, protests, and even the resignation of the Greek Prime Minister. By forcing Greece to implement drastic cuts to public services and social welfare programs, the IMF effectively undermined the country's ability to govern itself, demonstrating the dangers of unchecked global economic institutions imposing their will on sovereign nations.",
